00:34:32,241 --> 00:34:33,240
you know?

534
00:34:33,241 --> 00:34:35,240
So...

535
00:34:35,241 --> 00:34:37,240
And it's that concern about safety

536
00:34:37,241 --> 00:34:40,240
that might limit dragsters from going much faster.

537
00:34:40,241 --> 00:34:43,240
Officials citing safety concerns

538
00:34:43,241 --> 00:34:47,240
have put restrictions on tires, fuel, engine size,

539
00:34:47,241 --> 00:34:51,240
gear ratios, and many other technologies.

540
00:34:51,241 --> 00:34:55,240
We're being confined to a certain playing field,

541
00:34:55,241 --> 00:34:59,240
so we're down to finding hundreds of a second or thousands

542
00:34:59,241 --> 00:35:01,240
of a second to increase our performance.

543
00:35:05,240 --> 00:35:07,240
So what does the future hold?

544
00:35:07,241 --> 00:35:12,240
Coming up, a leading designer unveils his latest machine

545
00:35:12,241 --> 00:35:16,240
that could take drag racing in a new direction.

546
00:35:17,240 --> 00:35:24,240
There are millions of four cylinder cars in the world,

547
00:35:24,241 --> 00:35:27,240
but so far, none like this.

548
00:35:32,240 --> 00:35:34,240
A standard streetcar with four cylinders

549
00:35:34,241 --> 00:35:37,240
has less than 200 horsepower.

550
00:35:42,240 --> 00:35:46,240
This still experimental dragster has four three

551
00:35:46,241 --> 00:35:48,940
has 4,000.

552
00:35:49,040 --> 00:35:52,740
It's built to go 250 miles an hour plus,

553
00:35:52,840 --> 00:35:56,380
and it's a glimpse into one future direction of dragster

554
00:35:56,480 --> 00:35:58,080
design.

555
00:35:58,180 --> 00:36:01,880
Its designer, Bob Norwood, says there's not much room left

556
00:36:01,980 --> 00:36:05,800
for innovation with today's top dragsters.

557
00:36:05,900 --> 00:36:09,800
He says the big V8 dragsters can't be improved much more

558
00:36:09,900 --> 00:36:11,940
because of safety rules.

559
00:36:12,040 --> 00:36:16,000
So he's taken the power technology of the dragster

560
00:36:16,001 --> 00:36:22,420
and combined it with the size and the look of today's most popular street racers,

561
00:36:23,080 --> 00:36:25,160
the Japanese four-cylinder cars.

562
00:36:25,900 --> 00:36:29,340
The result is a car he calls the Max 4.

563
00:36:30,440 --> 00:36:32,600
With that mindset, we came into this thing,

564
00:36:32,680 --> 00:36:34,640
let's just go out and start off with a small motor,

565
00:36:34,940 --> 00:36:37,140
which is a four-cylinder versus a V8,

566
00:36:37,660 --> 00:36:40,500
and it's going to have inherently less power because it's smaller,

567
00:36:40,600 --> 00:36:42,580
but we can put more technology back in it

568
00:36:42,581 --> 00:36:46,860
and get it to where it matches something like a car

569
00:36:46,861 --> 00:36:50,160
that you could buy today.

570
00:36:50,161 --> 00:36:53,060
On the outside, the Max 4 looks pretty similar

571
00:36:53,061 --> 00:36:56,400
to the streetcar it was modeled after.

572
00:36:56,401 --> 00:36:58,800
We started with a Honda Acro Integra body,

573
00:36:58,801 --> 00:37:00,460
and that's where our changes began.

574
00:37:00,461 --> 00:37:02,240
We started changing everything.

575
00:37:02,241 --> 00:37:04,340
We went 20 inches narrower.

576
00:37:04,341 --> 00:37:08,440
We added a 14-inch distance here to get the wheelbase out

577
00:37:08,441 --> 00:37:10,700
from 100 inches to 115.

578
00:37:10,701 --> 00:37:12,860
We made all Lexan windows and stuff for it

579
00:37:12,861 --> 00:37:15,500
and blocked off the doors so you don't see the door handles

580
00:37:15,501 --> 00:37:16,520
or any of the doors or anything.

581
00:37:16,760 --> 00:37:18,140
This is where the exhaust comes out.

582
00:37:18,600 --> 00:37:20,680
These air vents that flip up under high pressure

583
00:37:20,681 --> 00:37:21,620
to let the air out.

584
00:37:23,040 --> 00:37:24,120
Two parachutes.

585
00:37:24,320 --> 00:37:25,940
When we got it all done, this is the only part

586
00:37:25,941 --> 00:37:28,940
that was the original part, and that's the decal on the back.

587
00:37:30,420 --> 00:37:34,360
But underneath, the Max 4 is anything but a streetcar.

588
00:37:34,820 --> 00:37:37,960
It's an updated version of ProDragster technology.

589
00:37:37,961 --> 00:37:41,960
Basically, this is the whole fuel system in this part of the deal.

590
00:37:41,961 --> 00:37:44,960
The cam belts and cam drives and the cam towers.

591
00:37:44,961 --> 00:37:46,960
Spark plugs, three for each cylinder.

592
00:37:46,961 --> 00:37:49,960
These are the turbochargers, exhaust manifolds.

593
00:37:49,961 --> 00:37:50,960
This box is the steering box.

594
00:37:50,961 --> 00:37:51,960
It's always in gear.

595
00:37:51,961 --> 00:37:52,960
It has only one gear.

596
00:37:52,961 --> 00:37:53,960
There's no transmission.

597
00:37:53,961 --> 00:37:55,960
The brakes are run by hand.

598
00:37:55,961 --> 00:37:56,960
This is the brake.

599
00:37:56,961 --> 00:38:04,960
Solid, smooth rubber tires, 17 inches wide, and a rear end, final drive here, which is

600
00:38:04,961 --> 00:38:11,460
It's a 3.2 gear ratio that runs a big titanium axle shaft

601
00:38:11,461 --> 00:38:12,460
that drives the wheels.

602
00:38:15,700 --> 00:38:18,200
There are already classes of four-cylinder cars

603
00:38:18,201 --> 00:38:19,600
on the pro circuit.

604
00:38:19,601 --> 00:38:24,020
They hit top speeds of around 190 over the quarter mile.

605
00:38:24,021 --> 00:38:27,520
Norwood projects that his car will eventually go 250

606
00:38:27,521 --> 00:38:32,460
and cover the distance in less than six seconds.

607
00:38:32,461 --> 00:38:36,160
One reason is the huge engine block that dwarfs other four

608
00:38:36,161 --> 00:38:37,600
cylinder blocks.

609
00:38:37,601 --> 00:38:43,740
It has a capacity of 286 cubic inches, or 4.8 liters,

610
00:38:43,741 --> 00:38:47,840
and is cut from a solid chunk of aluminum.

611
00:38:47,841 --> 00:38:49,740
This engine is not liquid cooled at all.

612
00:38:49,741 --> 00:38:52,520
It has no oil drains going back through all the oil

613
00:38:52,521 --> 00:38:54,120
drains on the outside.

614
00:38:54,121 --> 00:38:55,240
And so it's solid.

615
00:38:55,241 --> 00:38:56,920
It's that thick.

616
00:38:56,921 --> 00:38:59,280
And it's just a piece of aluminum that thick

617
00:38:59,281 --> 00:39:00,360
has got a lot of strength.

618
00:39:00,361 --> 00:39:03,700
That's what we need is a good, strong case

619
00:39:03,701 --> 00:39:07,200
to hold all the parts so it can take the huge horsepower,

620
00:39:07,201 --> 00:39:08,200
4,000 horsepower.

621
00:39:11,200 --> 00:39:15,300
Perhaps the biggest innovation is the fuel system.

622
00:39:15,301 --> 00:39:18,120
Like the top drag cars, the MAX 4

623
00:39:18,121 --> 00:39:21,020
runs on powerful nitromethane.

624
00:39:21,021 --> 00:39:24,360
But instead of premixing the nitro with alcohol,

625
00:39:24,361 --> 00:39:27,420
this car has two separate fuel tanks.

626
00:39:27,421 --> 00:39:32,420
Onboard computers decide when to use each fuel.

627
00:39:32,520 --> 00:39:34,920
This is an alcohol tank, and this tank

628
00:39:35,020 --> 00:39:36,460
contains the nitromethane.

629
00:39:36,560 --> 00:39:39,760
There's a small battery which runs the two computers.

630
00:39:39,860 --> 00:39:43,000
This computer on the top runs the ignition and the nitro,

631
00:39:43,100 --> 00:39:44,940
and the computer on the bottom runs the alcohol

632
00:39:45,040 --> 00:39:46,640
and does all the data logging.

633
00:39:49,400 --> 00:39:54,040
Norwood says his system will cut the fuel costs in half

634
00:39:54,041 --> 00:39:57,540
and greatly reduce the risk of nitro explosions

635
00:39:57,541 --> 00:40:00,640
inside the engine.

636
00:40:00,641 --> 00:40:02,840
We start the engine on alcohol, and then after we're

637
00:40:02,841 --> 00:40:05,780
ready to run, we're just ready to stage the car.

638
00:40:05,781 --> 00:40:08,580
We turn on the nitro methane.

639
00:40:08,581 --> 00:40:11,400
As we go down the track, we're going to roll out the nitro

640
00:40:11,401 --> 00:40:13,600
at about the 1,000-foot mark and run a bunch of alcohol

641
00:40:13,601 --> 00:40:15,400
to that last 300 feet.

642
00:40:15,401 --> 00:40:18,700
It keeps the engine from getting killed in the process.

643
00:40:18,701 --> 00:40:19,800
Nation on.

644
00:40:19,801 --> 00:40:31,640
The hard part is finding exactly how and when to switch between fuels.

645
00:40:31,641 --> 00:40:36,240
A hundredth of a second could make all the difference.

646
00:40:36,241 --> 00:40:40,240
If I want to add some fuel, say right there, then what I do is I just go like this.

647
00:40:40,241 --> 00:40:44,160
That's more fuel, this is less fuel.

648
00:40:44,161 --> 00:40:47,920
We do our tuning with a, instead of a screwdriver

649
00:40:47,921 --> 00:40:50,600
changing jets, we just deal with a computer right here.

650
00:40:50,601 --> 00:40:53,700
Now I'm just rich in that mixture up right there in that spot.

651
00:40:53,701 --> 00:40:57,060
It's just a learning curve, and it's a steeple.

652
00:40:57,061 --> 00:41:00,440
Norwood says the Max 4, once he's finished tweaking it,

653
00:41:00,441 --> 00:41:03,960
will sell for around $100,000 for the whole car,

654
00:41:03,961 --> 00:41:06,420
and that running costs will be about a quarter of those

655
00:41:06,421 --> 00:41:07,520
of a top dragster.

656
00:41:07,521 --> 00:41:13,280
Thought he'd give you a good pop.

657
00:41:15,720 --> 00:41:20,620
Some of the Max Force technologies are currently not allowed in pro drag racing.

658
00:41:21,120 --> 00:41:26,780
For example, computer-driven fuel injection and boosting the turbochargers with nitrous oxide,

659
00:41:27,320 --> 00:41:30,700
a powerful gas once used in fighter aircraft.

660
00:41:31,200 --> 00:41:35,020
But Bob thinks the rules will eventually catch up with the technology.

661
00:41:35,021 --> 00:41:38,120
I thought, you know, this is going to be a no rules type

662
00:41:38,220 --> 00:41:39,020
deal.

663
00:41:39,120 --> 00:41:40,420
There is not a class for it.

664
00:41:40,520 --> 00:41:42,620
It's going to be a purely exhibition type car

665
00:41:42,720 --> 00:41:44,420
right at this point in the game.

666
00:41:44,520 --> 00:41:51,480
But it looks to me as something that is potentially going to

667
00:41:51,580 --> 00:41:52,480
happen.

668
00:41:52,580 --> 00:41:56,380
And if nothing else, I'll be the first guy that ever did this.

669
00:42:02,480 --> 00:42:04,320
Drag racing has always been about

